            "paragraph": "For a given number of elements, the first two methods result in the same size of the linear system, whereas for the third, just half the size of the linear system is needed. Nevertheless, we established that in order to maintain the quality of the solution, the number of elements should be increased for the last method. The first two methods lead to the same results in the case of linear (or plane) boundaries (as for experiments A, B, C and D), but the number of mesh nodes for the bubbles is half compared to the Taylor-Hood method, such that tests A, B, C, D and F were performed using the bubble stabilisation method.",
